    "created_at": "2021-05-17T20:43:22Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-05-17T20:43:22Z",
    "body": "I think double-encoded labels must be considered invalid. I see two ways to achieve this:\r\n1. Set *CheckHyphens* to true\r\n2. Or modify [UTS 46 validity criteria](https://www.unicode.org/reports/tr46/#Validity_Criteria): add following criteria (suppose after 3):\r\n   \"If *CheckHyphens* = false, the label must not begin with `xn--`\"",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
