    "updated_at": "2021-05-17T23:01:33Z",
    "body": "@rmisev Indeed! As evident in UTS 46, the _CheckHyphens_ boolean was first introduced to allow YouTube labels of form \"r3---sn-apo3qvuoxuxbt-j5pe\". (Previously the boolean was effectively always \"true\".) But I suppose the Unicode folks didn't consider the possibility of `xn--`, which now needs to be forbidden explicitly.",
