    "body": "> This is somewhat important because Firefox can create such double-encoded labels:\r\n> \r\n> ```js\r\n> » new URL('http://xn--é').hostname\r\n> ❮ \"xn--xn---epa\"\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThat is no longer the case. Firefox now throws for `new URL('http://xn--é')`",
